00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 241828 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 1228 PM MDT Mon Aug 24 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - This week will see daily afternoon thunderstorm chances, particularly along the higher terrain of western Colorado and eastern Utah. - Localized heavy rainfall continues to pose a threat to flash flooding over burn scars and susceptible terrain. - Daytime","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-08-24T18:35:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION... Moisture decreases this week, but enough remains in place to keep mountain showers and thunderstorms in the forecast each afternoon. The potential for localized heavy rainfall keeps flash flood and debris flow concerns elevated for newer burn scars and areas of susceptible terrain. Other concerns with afternoon convection include lightning and gusty outflow winds near or above 35 mp","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=FWF&format=CI"},"coagmet":{"station_id":"orm02","station_name":"CSU Orchard Mesa Research Station","distance_km":12.3,"soil_temp_5cm_f":83.44,"soil_temp_15cm_f":79.66,"soil_moisture_5cm":null,"soil_moisture_15cm":null,"precip_in":null,"eto_in":null,"vapor_pressure":null,"solar_radiation":110.28,"wind_speed_mph":5.4,"air_temp_f":83.64,"relative_humidity":0.308,"url":"https://coagmet.colostate.edu/station/orm02"},"aviation":{"icao":"KGJT","distance_km":0,"raw_metar":"METAR KGJT 242153Z 17006KT 10SM CLR 33/08 A3016 RMK AO2 LTG DSNT SW SLP135 T03280083","temp_f":91,"wind_dir":170,"wind_kt":6,"gust_kt":null,"visibility":"10+","cover":"CLR","flight_category":"VFR","altimeter":1021.4,"observed":1787608380,"raw_taf":"TAF KGJT 241720Z 2418/2518 10011KT P6SM FEW120 FEW250 FM241900 27008KT P6SM BKN250 FM242300 33007KT P6SM FEW120 FEW250 FM250300 07007KT P6SM FEW120 FEW250","url":"https://aviationweather.gov/data/metar/?ids